WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.119 --> 00:00:06.350
The horrifically dystopian Squid Game is filled
with sneaky clues and easter eggs that predict

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:11.040
the Front Man's real identity, all the major
character deaths, and hint to some theories

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.889
on what to expect from a second season.

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:18.439
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing over 45 twisted details

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:20.419
you might have missed in Squid Game.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:22.580
Spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.380
Although the mysterious Front Man who oversees
the games remains hidden behind a mask till

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.430
late in the series, the show does give us
a tantalising clue early on to his true identity

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.839
as policeman Jun-ho's missing brother.

00:00:34.839 --> 00:00:40.309
When Jun-ho visits his sibling's apartment
in episode 2, you'll see he's heavily into

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:41.309
art, and among his books are several on Picasso,
who co-founded the Cubist movement.

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:44.899
That's crucial because, if you look at the
Front Man, you'll see how his interest in

00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:47.420
Cubism has influenced him and his surroundings.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:53.089
For example, look out for objects fractured
into geometrical angular shapes with concave

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:57.739
or convex surfaces, the idea of that look
in Cubism was to show objects from multiple

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:01.289
perspectives at the same time rather than
just one.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:05.430
When Gi-hun, Sae-byeok and Sang-woo make it
to the final round, they're served a final

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.870
meal which the creator has said is meant to
look like the Last Supper.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:13.370
For Gi-hun though, when the steak is revealed,
the moment is especially significant because

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:17.480
his daughter was taken to a steakhouse by
her stepfather for her birthday.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:21.830
Prior to the Games, Gi-hun had also planned
to treat her to an expensive meal, but after

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:26.600
losing his winnings could only afford something
much cheaper, so getting a plate of steak

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.810
at this point feels particularly ironic.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:33.340
And this might be a bit of a stretch, but
some fans have suspected the stepfather who

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.610
is also Gi-hun's nemesis may be connected
in some way to the Games so this steak may

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.090
hint at that.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:43.930
Also notice how the three tables are set out
in a triangular shape.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.110
And these are on a large circle filled with
black-and-white squares.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:51.190
So the entire layout is made up of the three
Squid Game symbols:

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.700
a circle, a triangle and a square.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.160
One of the three survivors at this point is
Sang-woo and there's some foreshadowing of

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.960
this moment in the second episode when his
mother was talking to him on the phone and

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.650
she was interrupted by a customer asking for
three squids.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:09.700
Some other hidden squid references and symbols
in the series include the hairclip in the

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.480
shape of the Squid Game logo on the giant
Robo-Doll's head.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:18.350
The elevator entrance to the Front Man's room
has intersecting circles, triangles and a

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.569
square shape.

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:24.540
The guards are organised into three types
by the squid game symbols on their masks,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.900
and the squid game logo is always highlighted
in the guard's hot pink uniform colour in

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.900
the show's title.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.310
One of the brilliant things about the series
is how it manages to get you invested in lots

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:39.120
of characters even though we know are going
to die because of the very nature of the game.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.609
And many of those deaths are intriguingly
telegraphed early on.

00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:46.909
The way Mi-nyeo dies as she grabs hold of
Deok-su, leans back and falls through the

00:02:46.909 --> 00:02:51.530
glass was foreshowed back in the tug-of-war
game when she commented that leaning back

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:54.140
made her feel so much more powerful.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.709
Deok-su also foreshadowed his death in the
second episode when he jumped off a bridge

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:00.739
to escape from his enemies.

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:05.370
Jun-ho's death as he falls into the sea mirrors
how he dumped the Squid Game worker's body

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.400
after stealing his identity so he could go
undercover in the game.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.439
Ali's heart-breaking death when he discovers
that Sang-Woo has cheated him out of his bag

00:03:13.439 --> 00:03:18.480
of marbles, echoes how he stole a packet of
cash from his boss who owed him money.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.260
Sae-byeok dies with her throat slit by Sang-woo,
the thing she threatened to do to the guy

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.469
who lost the money she gave him to help get
her family out of North Korea.

00:03:27.469 --> 00:03:31.780
And if you look closely, you can also spot
a scar already on her neck, another bit of

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.849
foreshadowing for her fate.

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:37.840
And Sang-Woo kills himself at the end, like
he almost did when the police were tracking

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.489
him down in the second episode.

00:03:39.489 --> 00:03:44.420
There's a popular theory about the red and
blue tile game which posits that players who

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:49.230
choose a blue tile go on to become participants
in the game, whereas those who choose a red

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.000
tile become the jumpsuit-wearing workers.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.819
The original inspiration for the Salesman's
game is very creepy and based on a Korean

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:59.610
urban legend called Red Tissue, Blue Tissue.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:04.200
Which is itself based on a Japanese horror
story where a ghost appears to people using

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.409
a public bathroom and offers them red or blue
toilet paper.

00:04:07.409 --> 00:04:11.900
There are many variations of the story, but
those who choose red are generally killed

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:17.139
in a gruesome, bloody fashion, whereas those
choosing blue are suffocated to death.

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:21.920
The giant killer robot in the bone-chilling
challenge Red Light, Green Light is based

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:26.310
on a character who featured in Korean primary
school books used to teach children how to

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.940
read in the 70s and 80s.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:33.400
And we see that same shocking contrast between
the games' childhood origins and the brutal

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.389
adult contest in the show's brightly coloured
sets and costumes, which give the competition

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:42.310
a child-like fairy-tale feel or strange fantasy
vibe.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:47.400
A recurring theme in the show is how The Blue
Danube is played over the loudspeakers just

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:52.870
before each of the deadly games is about to
start.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:59.770
The famous waltz by Johann Strauss Jr becomes
a terrible harbinger of what's to come,

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:03.940
and the incongruously light-hearted nature
of the music is completely at odds with the

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:08.230
deception, death, and destruction that awaits
the players in every game.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:15.740
It even plays during the final trio's last
supper, adding to the horrific nature of the

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.259
situation.

00:05:17.259 --> 00:05:21.449
The Blue Danube was originally written to
help lift the mood of the Austrian nation

00:05:21.449 --> 00:05:26.550
in the 1860s after the country had lost a
war, was economically depressed, and morale

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.050
was generally low.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:32.610
And the Squid Games organisers may be trying
to use this upbeat tune in a similar way to

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:37.550
encourage the players who are in financial
straits to raise their spirits and keep playing.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:42.470
The music is also used in this amazing shot
from above where the players move along MC

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:47.860
Escher-inspired stairs, with their seemingly
endless motion around the spiral-style staircase

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.720
reminiscent of the constant turns of the Viennese
waltz.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.910
The trippy look and disorienting design of
the staircases is also a deliberate homage

00:05:55.910 --> 00:06:00.979
to Escher's art piece "Relativity" in which
the usual laws of gravity don't make sense,

00:06:00.979 --> 00:06:05.220
an analogy perhaps for the horrific reality
of the Squid Games.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:09.650
When many players announce they want to abandon
ship after the Red Light massacre, the prize

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:14.509
money they'll end up forfeiting is announced,
and as the cash drops into a massive Perspex

00:06:14.509 --> 00:06:19.780
piggy bank, it's accompanied by the sound
of a chiptune.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:23.430
Similar music played during the scene in the
first episode where Gi-hun tried to win a

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:26.689
present at the arcade for his daughter's birthday.

00:06:26.689 --> 00:06:30.490
Another horrifying connection between the
arcade and the Squid Games is that the prize

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:35.020
Gi-hun wins for his daughter comes wrapped
in a black box with a bow, similar to the

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.590
coffins used for disposing of dead bodies
in the Squid Games.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:43.449
Check out the multiple pictures the Front
Man has in his old apartment of a dark street

00:06:43.449 --> 00:06:46.419
at night underneath a bright blue, sunlit
sky .

00:06:46.419 --> 00:06:51.720
They're from the Empire of Light collection
by surrealist artist René Magritte and inspired

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.330
this iconic scene in The Exorcist.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:58.990
Like so much in the Squid Games, they point
to the unsettling and upsetting contrasts

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:02.250
of the show's world, where kids' games have
deadly consequences,

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:07.080
and brothers who once sacrificed a kidney
to save your life, end up shooting you off

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.650
a cliff to your death.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.349
By the way, if you were intrigued by the Front
Man's character but wanted to know more, the

00:07:12.349 --> 00:07:17.000
show's creator has said a potential Season
2 might explore his story in greater detail

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.770
while also including more on the police.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:24.020
The VIP episode makes it clear that there
are Squid Games happening in other parts of

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.020
the world..

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.860
The contest in Korea was the best.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:32.520
..meaning the secret network that runs the
diabolical enterprise must be relatively extensive.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:36.580
And in the final episode, the meeting that
Gi-hun has with his bank manager reveals a

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:40.419
clue that the bank itself or its manager may
also be involved.

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:46.020
The hint is in how the bank employee mentions
they have a VIP-only service for wealthy individuals

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.020
like Gi-hun.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:52.669
The term VIP here seems specific and could
suggest Gi-hun is being offered the opportunity

00:07:52.669 --> 00:07:55.069
to become an observer at the games should
he wish.

00:07:55.069 --> 00:07:59.540
After all, Il-nam mentioned on his death bed
that he started the games with other people

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:04.099
who like him were basically bored despite
being hugely rich.

00:08:04.099 --> 00:08:08.379
The deposit of so much money into Gi-hun's
account would also, under money laundering

00:08:08.379 --> 00:08:12.169
rules, likely trigger an investigation into
the source of the funds, and this doesn't

00:08:12.169 --> 00:08:13.860
appear to have happened.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:18.020
It's also suspicious that Jun-ho's call to
the Korean Police just before he was killed

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:21.849
hasn't resulted in anything;
after all, the location of his call could

00:08:21.849 --> 00:08:23.629
have been easily traced by his boss.

00:08:23.629 --> 00:08:29.110
It could simply be police incompetence;
however, it could also suggest there are higher-ups

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:33.430
in his police department who've been paid
off by the Squid Games not to investigate

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:36.769
the yearly disappearances of hundreds of people.

00:08:36.769 --> 00:08:41.290
A twisted detail that was deliberately hidden
from players is that, from the start, all

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:45.410
six games to be played were depicted on the
walls of the dorm area.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.750
In the beginning, these were obscured by the
players' bunk beds.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.470
And although knowing what the games would
be would have given everyone much better odds

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:57.500
of survival, it's only as more and more players
are killed off that the true nature of each

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.500
game is revealed.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:02.800
I think the added meaning here is that, despite
all the Front Man's claims that the Games

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:07.540
are fair, the truth is intentionally hidden
from participants and only revealed to the

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.519
few who make it to the end.

00:09:09.519 --> 00:09:13.620
Another example of the injustice of those
in charge of the system is when Ali goes to

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:18.520
claim his unpaid wages and finds his boss
playing a computer game rather than trying

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:21.600
to fix his business so he can pay his workers.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.360
Just like the VIPs in charge of the Squid
Games, Ali's boss is only interested in his

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:28.700
own entertainment at the expense of others.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:33.459
So, did you spot any other interesting details
or easter eggs in Squid Game?

00:09:33.459 --> 00:09:37.580
And what do you think was the most horrifying
or heart-breaking moment in the show?

